concept_understand("S22 · Concept 2 · [THEORY] [SNIPPET]","Data / Domain Types",
    "A data type is the DOMAIN of a column — the set of values it may hold. Choosing the right type enforces correctness and saves space. Core MySQL types: INT, DECIMAL(p,s), VARCHAR(n)/CHAR(n), DATE, BOOLEAN.",
    ["INT — whole numbers (roll, credits). DECIMAL(10,2) — exact money (NPR fees).",
     "VARCHAR(n) — variable-length text up to n; CHAR(n) — fixed length, padded.",
     "DATE — calendar dates (dob); BOOLEAN — true/false flags.",
     "Never store money as FLOAT — binary rounding corrupts fee/amount totals."],
    None,"Data type = the size of tiffin box — wrong size wastes space or won't fit.",
    "~9 min. Phone numbers are VARCHAR, not INT (leading 0 in 98XXXXXXXX, and '+977'). Money is DECIMAL, not FLOAT.")
