# ============================================================ S32
add_divider("Session 32 · Lecture hour 11 (of 15)","Update of a View (Updatable vs Non-Updatable)",
    "You built the BIMStudents view yesterday. Can you INSERT a new student THROUGH it? Sometimes yes, sometimes the database says no — why?",
    "OPENING HOOK [~5 min]. Agenda: modifying through a view → updatability rules → non-updatable views → WITH CHECK OPTION. Pin the schema.")

concept_understand("S32 · Concept 1 · [THEORY]","Modifying Through a View",
    "Changes to a SIMPLE view can pass through to its base table: an UPDATE/INSERT/DELETE on the view modifies the underlying rows. This works only when the mapping from view rows to base rows is unambiguous.",
    ["UPDATE BIMStudents SET semester=5 WHERE roll=101; updates the Student table.",
     "The view must map each of its rows to exactly one base-table row.",
     "Simple column/row subsets of ONE table are the updatable case.",
     "The DBMS rewrites the view modification into a base-table modification."],
    None,"A simple view is a clear window — changes pass straight through the glass to the table.",
    "~7 min. Show UPDATE BIMStudents actually changing Student. Set up the 'sometimes it's blocked' tension.")
add_table_slide("S32 · Concept 1 · examples","Does the modification pass through the view?",
    ["View","Modification","Passes through?"],
    [["BIMStudents (filter of Student)","UPDATE … SET semester=5","yes — one base row per view row"],
     ["BIMStudents","INSERT a new BIM student","yes (needs the NOT NULL cols)"],
     ["PublicInstructor (name, dept only)","UPDATE dept","yes — single table subset"],
     ["MeritList (Student JOIN Enrollment)","UPDATE marks","ambiguous / blocked (join)"],
     ["DeptAvgSalary (GROUP BY dept)","UPDATE avg_salary","no — aggregate can't map back"],
     ["a view with a computed column","UPDATE that column","no — derived value"]],
    per_page=6,widths=[2.6,2.2,2.1],fs=10.5,
    note="A modification passes through only when the DBMS can map each view row to exactly one base-table row. Single-table filters/subsets qualify; joins, aggregates, and computed columns generally do not.")
concept_apply("S32 · Concept 1 · [THEORY]","Modifying Through a View",
    "An admin panel often exposes an editable view rather than the raw table. Editing a student's semester in the BIMStudents view writes straight through to the Student table — the coordinator never touches the base table directly, but their save still lands there.",
    "\"Editing a view only changes the view, not the real data.\" For an updatable view, the change passes THROUGH to the base table — the view has no data of its own. If it were non-updatable, the save would be rejected instead.",
    "Modifying a view means running INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE against it; for an updatable view the DBMS rewrites this into a modification of the underlying base table, since the view stores no data. This works only when each view row maps unambiguously to exactly one base-table row.",
    "modify through view · pass-through to base table · unambiguous row mapping · views store no data")

concept_understand("S32 · Concept 2 · [THEORY]","Updatable Views — the Rules",
    "A view is updatable when it maps cleanly to one base table: built on a SINGLE table, no aggregates/DISTINCT/GROUP BY, no derived (computed) columns, and it includes the base table's required NOT NULL columns (so an INSERT can supply them).",
    ["Single base table (no joins).",
     "No GROUP BY, aggregate functions, or DISTINCT.",
     "No derived/computed columns in the SELECT list.",
     "Includes the NOT NULL columns needed to insert a valid base row."],
    "s32_updatable.png","Updatable = simple, single-table, no summarising, no computed columns.",
    "~9 min. BIMStudents (a simple filter of Student) is updatable. Walk the checklist against it.")
add_table_slide("S32 · Concept 2 · scaffolding","The updatability checklist — pass all to be updatable",
    ["Rule","Updatable view","Non-updatable if…"],
    [["Single base table","one table only","it joins two+ tables"],
     ["No aggregates","plain columns","it uses SUM/AVG/COUNT…"],
     ["No GROUP BY / DISTINCT","row-for-row","it groups or de-duplicates"],
     ["No computed columns","stored columns only","it has marks*1.0 etc."],
     ["Includes NOT NULL cols","can insert a valid row","required columns are missing"],
     ["Example","BIMStudents","DeptAvgSalary, MeritList"]],
    per_page=6,widths=[2.1,2.2,2.2],fs=10.5,
    note="All boxes must be ticked. A view fails updatability the moment it joins, aggregates, groups, de-duplicates, or computes — because the DBMS can no longer map a view row to one base row.")
concept_apply("S32 · Concept 2 · [THEORY]","Updatable Views — the Rules",
    "BIMStudents = SELECT roll,name,program,semester FROM Student WHERE program='BIM' is updatable: one table, no aggregates, no computed columns, and it carries the NOT NULL columns, so you can UPDATE or even INSERT a BIM student through it.",
    "\"Any view can be edited like a table.\" Only views meeting the updatability rules — single table, no aggregates/DISTINCT/GROUP BY, no derived columns, and the required NOT NULL columns present. Break any rule and the DBMS rejects the modification.",
    "A view is updatable when it maps cleanly to a single base table: no joins, no aggregates/GROUP BY/DISTINCT, no derived columns, and it includes the base table's NOT NULL columns so inserts can supply them. Only then can the DBMS translate a view modification into an unambiguous base-table modification.",
    "updatable view · single table · no aggregate/GROUP BY/DISTINCT · no derived columns · NOT NULL present")

concept_understand("S32 · Concept 3 · [THEORY]","Non-Updatable Views & WITH CHECK OPTION",
    "Views with joins, aggregates, GROUP BY, or computed columns are generally NON-updatable — the change can't be mapped back to base rows unambiguously. WITH CHECK OPTION guards an updatable view so you can't insert/update a row that falls OUTSIDE the view's filter.",
    ["DeptAvgSalary (GROUP BY dept) — 'raise the average to 80k' is meaningless per row → non-updatable.",
     "A join view — which base table would an insert go into? → ambiguous, blocked.",
     "WITH CHECK OPTION: inserting a 'BCA' student through BIMStudents WITH CHECK OPTION is rejected.",
     "It stops rows 'disappearing' from a view the moment they're inserted."],
    None,"You can't un-bake a cake: an aggregate view can't be pushed back into individual rows.",
    "~9 min. DeptAvgSalary is non-updatable. Then WITH CHECK OPTION blocks inserting a BCA row via BIMStudents.")
add_table_slide("S32 · Concept 3 · examples","Non-updatable views and the CHECK OPTION guard",
    ["View / clause","Why non-updatable / what it guards","Attempted change"],
    [["DeptAvgSalary (GROUP BY dept)","aggregate can't map to rows","'set avg=80k' — meaningless"],
     ["MeritList (Student JOIN Enrollment)","which base table gets the change?","UPDATE marks — ambiguous"],
     ["Pct (marks*1.0 AS pct)","derived column has no base storage","UPDATE pct — impossible"],
     ["a DISTINCT view","de-dup loses row identity","UPDATE a merged row — ambiguous"],
     ["BIMStudents WITH CHECK OPTION","guards the filter (program='BIM')","INSERT a 'BCA' row — REJECTED"],
     ["BIMStudents WITH CHECK OPTION","guards the filter","UPDATE program to 'BCA' — REJECTED"]],
    per_page=6,widths=[2.5,2.6,2.0],fs=10.5,
    note="Joins/aggregates/DISTINCT/computed columns break the row mapping → non-updatable. WITH CHECK OPTION keeps an updatable view honest: it forbids changes that would put a row outside the view's own condition.")
concept_apply("S32 · Concept 3 · [THEORY]","Non-Updatable Views & WITH CHECK OPTION",
    "A DeptAvgSalary view (GROUP BY dept) can't be updated — 'raise this department's average to 80k' has no single-row meaning. And BIMStudents WITH CHECK OPTION rejects inserting a BCA student, so a row can't vanish from the very view you inserted it through.",
    "\"If a view won't save my change, it's a bug.\" Often it's correct behaviour: aggregated/joined views are non-updatable by design, and WITH CHECK OPTION deliberately blocks rows that would fall outside the view's filter. Understanding this prevents 'why won't my save go through?' confusion.",
    "Views built on joins, aggregates, GROUP BY, DISTINCT, or computed columns are generally non-updatable, because a change cannot be mapped back to base rows unambiguously (e.g. you can't push an average back to individual salaries). WITH CHECK OPTION protects an updatable view by rejecting inserts/updates that would place a row outside the view's defining condition.",
    "non-updatable · joins/aggregates/DISTINCT/computed · WITH CHECK OPTION · guard the filter")

